repository-code: "https://github.com/PureTearsDropped/equivalent-logic-physical-cost"
license: 0BSD
abstract: >-
  Functionally equivalent implementations of an exact unsigned 4x4 multiplier are
  compared under real physical cost on the SkyWater SKY130 standard-cell library:
  cell-level NLDM timing (validated against OpenSTA within 1.5%), OpenROAD/LibreLane
  placement and routing with parasitic extraction, and glitch-inclusive energy per
  operation from SDF-annotated gate-level simulation. A whole-DAG timing-driven
  optimizer decides gate duplication, drive strength, and full/half-adder variant
  selection from the full cell vocabulary; every candidate is verified exhaustively
  (256/256). Findings: the 9-NAND full adder is the fastest on SKY130; whole-DAG
  duplication keeps a 4.8% post-layout delay gain that OpenROAD's own resizer does not
  find; the standard synthesis flow reaches 10% lower delay only at 3.5x area and 6x
  energy per operation; OpenSTA's probabilistic power estimate over-counts by
  1.3-2.2x with a design-dependent factor and mis-ranks designs; and yosys/abc
  collapses every variant to the same 80-LUT FPGA mapping. Retracted intermediate
  claims are recorded rather than removed.
keywords:
  - logic synthesis
  - standard cells
  - sky130
  - OpenROAD
  - OpenSTA
  - static timing analysis
  - gate duplication
  - power estimation
  - glitch power
  - exact multiplier
  - Lean 4
  - carry-save
  - correctly rounded exp
  - pipelining
